#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:1
msgid "Instructions for *ACL Proceedings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:3
msgid ""
"The following instructions are for authors of papers submitted for review"
" to ACL conferences (hereafter, \"review version\") or paper accepted for"
" publication in its proceedings (hereafter, \"final version\"). All "
"authors are required to adhere to these specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:6
msgid "Style Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:8
msgid ""
"*ACL provides style files for LaTeX and Microsoft Word that meet these "
"requirements. They can be found at:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:10
msgid "https://acl-org.github.io/ACLPUB/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:12
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend the use of these style files, which have been "
"appropriately tailored for the *ACL proceedings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:14
msgid "Paper Length"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:16
msgid ""
"The conference accepts submissions of long papers and short papers. "
"Review versions of long papers may have up to eight (8) pages of content "
"plus unlimited pages for references. Upon acceptance, final versions of "
"long papers will be given one additional page -- up to nine (9) pages of "
"content plus unlimited pages for acknowledgements and references -- so "
"that reviewers' comments can be taken into account. Review versions of "
"short papers may have up to four (4) pages of content, plus unlimited "
"pages for references. Final versions of short papers may have up to five "
"(5) pages, plus unlimited pages for acknowledgements and references. For "
"both long and short papers, all figures and tables that are part of the "
"main text must fit within these page limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:23
msgid ""
"The conference encourages submission of appendices and supplementary "
"material, which are not required to fit within these page limits. "
"However, review versions of papers must be self-contained: it is optional"
" for reviewers to look at appendices or supplementary material. Please "
"see [Appendices](#Appendices) and [Supplementary](#Supplementary "
"Material) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:25
msgid ""
"Review versions should not refer, for further detail, to documents, code "
"or data resources that are not available to the reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:27
msgid ""
"Papers that do not conform to these requirements may be rejected without "
"review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:29
msgid ""
"Workshop chairs may have different rules for allowed length and whether "
"appendices or supplementary materials are welcome. As always, the "
"respective call for papers is the authoritative source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:32
msgid "Anonymity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:34
msgid ""
"As reviewing will be double-blind, review versions must not include any "
"identifying information about the authors (such as names, affiliations, "
"or URLs). Self-references that reveal the author's identity, e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:37
msgid "We previously showed (Gusfield, 1997)..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:39
msgid "must be avoided, and anonymous citations, e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:41
msgid "We previously showed (Anonymous, 1997)..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:43
msgid "should also be avoided. Instead, use citations such as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:45
msgid "Gusfield (1997) previously showed..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:47
msgid "Review versions must not include acknowledgements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:49
msgid ""
"**Papers that do not conform to these requirements may be rejected "
"without review.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:51
msgid ""
"Any preliminary non-archival versions of submitted papers should be "
"listed in the submission form but not in the review version of the paper."
" Reviewers are generally aware that authors may present preliminary "
"versions of their work in other venues, but will not be provided the list"
" of previous presentations from the submission form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:54
msgid ""
"Once a paper has been accepted to the conference, the final version "
"should include the author's names and affiliations, and is allowed to use"
" self-references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:56
msgid "Multiple Submission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:58
msgid ""
"Papers that have been or will be submitted to other meetings or "
"publications must indicate this at submission time in the START "
"submission form, and must be withdrawn from the other venues if accepted "
"by *ACL. Authors of papers accepted for presentation at *ACL must notify "
"the program chairs by the deadline for final versions (\"camera-ready "
"deadline\") whether the paper will be presented. We will not accept for "
"publication or presentation any papers that overlap significantly in "
"content or results with papers that will be (or have been) published "
"elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:62
msgid ""
"Authors submitting more than one paper to *ACL must ensure that "
"submissions do not overlap significantly (>25%) with each other in "
"content or results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:64
msgid "Formatting Instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:66
msgid "File Format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:68
msgid ""
"Papers must be in Adobe Portable Document Format (PDF). Please make sure "
"that your PDF file embeds all necessary fonts (especially for tree "
"diagrams, symbols, and Asian languages). When you print or create the PDF"
" file, there is usually an option in your printer setup to include none, "
"all or just non-standard fonts. Please make sure that you select the "
"option of including *all* the fonts. **Before sending it, test your PDF "
"by printing it from a computer different from the one where it was "
"created.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:74
msgid ""
"Some word processors may generate very large PDF files, where each page "
"is rendered as an image. Such images may reproduce poorly. In this case, "
"try alternative ways to obtain the PDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:78
msgid ""
"All papers must use **A4 paper format** (21 cm x 29.7 cm). Papers must "
"not be submitted with any other paper size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:81
msgid ""
"If you cannot meet the above requirements, please contact the publication"
" chairs as soon as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:83
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:85
msgid "All text except for page numbers must fit within the margins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:87
msgid ""
"Review versions should have page numbers, centered in the bottom margin, "
"but **pages should not be numbered in the final version.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:89
msgid ""
"Manuscripts must be set in two columns. Exceptions to the two-column "
"format include the title, authors' names and complete addresses, which "
"must be centered at the top of the first page, and any full-width figures"
" or tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:92
msgid "The exact dimensions for a page on A4 paper are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:94
msgid "Left margin: 2.5 cm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:95
msgid "Right margin: 2.5 cm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:96
msgid "Top margin: 2.5 cm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:97
msgid "Bottom margin: 2.5 cm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:98
msgid "Column width: 7.7 cm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:99
msgid "Column height: 24.7 cm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:100
msgid "Gap between columns: 0.6 cm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:102
msgid ""
"In the review version, a ruler (line numbers in the left and right "
"margins of the article) should be printed, so that reviewers may comment "
"on particular lines in the paper. The ruler should not change the "
"appearance of any other content on the page. The final version should not"
" contain a ruler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:106
msgid "Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:108
msgid ""
"All text (except non-Latin scripts and mathematical formulas) should be "
"set in **Times Roman**. If Times Roman is unavailable, you may use "
"**Times New Roman** or **Computer Modern Roman.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md:111
msgid ""
"The following table specifies what font sizes and styles must be used for"
" each type of text in the manuscript."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "Type of Text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "Font Size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "paper title"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "15 pt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "bold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "author names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "12 pt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "author affiliation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "the word ``Abstract''"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "section titles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "subsection titles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "11 pt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
msgid "document text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_formatting.md
